  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A grey marker drawing in a spiral sketchbook of a desert valley full of tall cactuses with raised arms, under rounded mountains.",
    "description": "A square photograph of a spiral bound sketchbook page on a wooden table. A landscape in grey and black marker: rounded mountains along the top with a few tall cactuses on their slopes, a wide valley of rolling ground in the middle, and a crowd of cactuses in the foreground, each a tall body with raised arms and small spines, standing in pools of dark shadow. The cactuses are drawn with black outlines and the ground with loose grey shading.",
    "impression": "The cactuses finally get a home: a valley where dozens of them stand around with their arms up like a congregation. Each one casts a puddle of shadow that makes it look like it is melting. The direct marker ancestor of the Desertland paintings, and a quiet, companionable scene.",
